<h1>height-balanced binary search tree</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="heightBalancedTree.html"><em>height-balanced tree</em></a> which is also a <a href="binarySearchTree.html"><em>binary search tree</em></a>. It supports membership, insert, and delete operations in time <a href="logarithmic.html"><em>logarithmic</em></a> in the number of <a href="node.html"><em>nodes</em></a> in the tree.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="heightBalancedTree.html"><em>height-balanced tree</em></a>, <a href="binarySearchTree.html"><em>binary search tree</em></a>, <a href="balancedbitr.html"><em>balanced binary tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="avltree.html"><em>AVL tree</em></a>, <a href="redblack.html"><em>red-black tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

